<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Agustín Gamarra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1785">1785</a>–<a href="/years/1841">1841</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Agustín Gamarra was a Peruvian general and president from 1829 to 1833 and again from 1838 to 1841. A leading opponent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andres-de-santa-cruz">Andrés de Santa Cruz</a>, he was defeated by him in 1835 and fought the Peru-Bolivian Confederation from exile with Chilean support. After its fall in 1839 he reunited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, but he was killed invading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ingavi">Battle of Ingavi</a> in 1841.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/agustin-gamarra.jpg" alt="Agustín Gamarra" width="320" height="360" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Agustin_Gamarra.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
